Aim

To write a C program that checks whether a given string can be derived from the grammar:

S -> 0 A 1
A -> 0 A | 1 A | ε

(This grammar generates the language 0(0|1)*1 — every valid string starts with 0, ends with 1, with anything in between.)

Algorithm
Read the input string.
S -> 0 A 1 forces the first symbol to be 0; if not, reject immediately.
Scan the middle portion of the string (between first and last character). Since A -> 0A | 1A, each 0 or 1 encountered here is a valid application of one of these productions — print it as a derivation step.
Eventually A -> ε is applied, leaving only the trailing symbol.
S -> 0 A 1 also forces the last symbol to be 1 — check this against what's left.
If every step matched (first = 0, all middle symbols are 0/1, last = 1, length ≥ 2), the string is ACCEPTED; otherwise REJECTED.
